WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.716 --> 00:00:10.077
Welcome to my forest.

2
00:00:10.917 --> 00:00:13.719
It is autumn, so it is very wonderful here.

3
00:00:14.579 --> 00:00:19.062
All the animals, including squirrels like me, are busy getting ready for winter.

4
00:00:20.002 --> 00:00:24.405
Look around you and you will see that the leaves on the trees have changed colors.

5
00:00:25.365 --> 00:00:30.228
The maple trees have turned bright red, and the elm trees have turned brown and yellow.

6
00:00:33.248 --> 00:00:37.429
Have you ever wondered why the green leaves change into so many different colors?

7
00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:44.011
Well, in the spring and summer when the leaves are fresh, they are filled with something called chlorophyll.

8
00:00:44.952 --> 00:00:48.633
Chlorophyll is the natural coloring in the leaves that makes them green.

9
00:00:50.573 --> 00:00:53.954
In order to make food, trees need energy from the sun.

10
00:00:54.895 --> 00:00:58.836
Chlorophyll collects the energy from the sun and stores it in the leaves.

11
00:00:59.700 --> 00:01:05.082
The leaves use this energy to make a liquid sugar, called sap, that the trees use for food.

12
00:01:08.204 --> 00:01:12.986
The trees spend the spring and summer producing food so that they can grow bigger.

13
00:01:13.846 --> 00:01:19.669
During the summer months, the trees get taller and wider and they grow more branches and roots.

14
00:01:20.329 --> 00:01:26.052
But most importantly, the trees use their energy to grow nuts and fruits for animals like me to

15
00:01:26.132 --> 00:01:31.685
eat. At the end of the summer, things begin to change.

16
00:01:32.705 --> 00:01:36.846
It becomes cooler, and there is much less sunlight during the day.

17
00:01:37.806 --> 00:01:41.447
Chlorophyll needs the sunlight and cannot survive in the cold weather.

18
00:01:42.428 --> 00:01:47.489
So in the autumn when the weather becomes cool, the trees can no longer make chlorophyll.

19
00:01:48.349 --> 00:01:51.410
When this happens, the leaves lose their green color.

20
00:01:53.631 --> 00:01:58.212
When the green chlorophyll disappears, the leaves' other colors can be seen.

21
00:01:59.196 --> 00:02:03.838
Trees like elm, birch, and poplar show their yellow and light orange colors.

22
00:02:04.899 --> 00:02:11.202
These colors were in the leaves all summer, but because of the green chlorophyll, we could not see

23
00:02:11.242 --> 00:02:16.165
them. Some trees, however, get new bright colors in the fall.

24
00:02:16.905 --> 00:02:22.248
For example, maple trees turn bright red, and sumac trees turn dark red.

25
00:02:23.324 --> 00:02:28.486
These trees get their color from red pigments that build up in the leaves when the sap stops

26
00:02:28.566 --> 00:02:29.607
flowing in the fall.

27
00:02:30.567 --> 00:02:33.768
These pigments turn leaves red, pink, and even purple.

28
00:02:35.469 --> 00:02:38.350
This natural coloring occurs in trees and other plants.

29
00:02:39.231 --> 00:02:43.012
It gives some vegetables, like beets and radishes, their red color.

30
00:02:43.892 --> 00:02:47.094
It is also what makes some flower blossoms red and pink.

31
00:02:48.474 --> 00:02:52.376
The red pigments come into the leaves during cool, dry, sunny days.

32
00:02:53.424 --> 00:02:57.187
I love to go running through the trees, looking at all the colors.

33
00:02:58.268 --> 00:03:01.850
Even on the same tree, not all the leaves have the same color.

34
00:03:03.972 --> 00:03:09.115
On some trees, the top leaves are bright red, but the bottom leaves are almost yellow.

35
00:03:09.976 --> 00:03:12.358
This is because the top ones get more sun.

36
00:03:13.278 --> 00:03:18.422
On trees near a river, the leaves are not bright because trees that get lots of water do

37
00:03:18.482 --> 00:03:20.924
not usually have colorful leaves in the fall.

38
00:03:23.292 --> 00:03:28.313
But way up there on the top of a mountain, the leaves get lots of sun and little

39
00:03:28.353 --> 00:03:30.594
water, so they are very colorful.

40
00:03:31.934 --> 00:03:35.295
Even from year to year, the colors of the leaves change.

41
00:03:36.216 --> 00:03:40.597
When autumn is dry and cool, the leaves will have brilliant, shining colors.

42
00:03:41.477 --> 00:03:45.758
But when the autumn is cloudy and wet, the leaves will not be as beautiful.

43
00:03:48.079 --> 00:03:52.140
The autumn leaves are beautiful to look at, but they don't last very long.

44
00:03:52.916 --> 00:03:55.397
Without chlorophyll, the leaves cannot live.

45
00:03:56.338 --> 00:03:59.340
Soon the leaves must fall off the branches onto the ground.

46
00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:04.102
But this is good for squirrels because we love to play and jump in them.

47
00:04:05.743 --> 00:04:10.606
When all the leaves have fallen from the trees, the animals know that winter is coming.

48
00:04:11.446 --> 00:04:16.409
We hurry up and pack away all our food, and then we tuck ourselves in our little houses

49
00:04:16.829 --> 00:04:18.190
and go to sleep for the winter.

50
00:04:19.051 --> 00:04:20.972
The trees also sleep during the winter.

51
00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:28.242
Eventually the leaves that fall from the trees decay and turn into soil that is used during the

52
00:04:28.302 --> 00:04:31.122
following years as fertilizer for the trees.

53
00:04:32.163 --> 00:04:37.604
You see, one of the beautiful things about nature is that everything works in a cycle.

54
00:04:39.465 --> 00:04:42.445
The trees wake up in the spring with fresh new leaves.

55
00:04:43.446 --> 00:04:49.087
These leaves grow in the summer, fall in the autumn, and then are turned back into soil so

56
00:04:49.127 --> 00:04:51.168
that more leaves can grow the next spring.

57
00:04:52.448 --> 00:04:56.671
With the help of chlorophyll, the trees get bigger and stronger every year.
